Abstract = {Experiments designed by students at any level is a fun way to learn
   physics. Laboratory activities can help students acquire, integrate and
   construct knowledge in a friendly way. For the last 15 years, we have
   promoted experimental work as projects in theoretical courses. The
   enthusiasm students have shown, even though they have to spend many
   extra hours, contrasts their dislike for traditional laboratory courses
   where they follow recipes. In this paper, we present the original
   project and its influence in other courses and in new curricula. We will
