   illustrated. The new taxon is compared with A. carterae and A.
   madrensis, species with similar morphological characteristics. It is
   however easily differentiated from these two by having glabrous leaves
   and floral parts, a lobed nectar disc, and it is known only from
   southwestern Mexico. A comparative table and a distribution map of the
   three species are included.},
