Pages = {1023-1032},
Month = {SEP},
Abstract = {The diversity of araneomorph spiders in an ecoturistic tropical forest
   remnant of approximately 40 ha is described. A 1-ha plot with
   homogeneous vegetation was established. Six sampling methods covered all
   microhabitats, except tree canopy. Four expeditions were conducted from
   August 2011 to June 2012. In a total of 485 samples, 4,118 adult
   specimens representing 205 morphospecies were collected. Nonparametric
   richness estimates varied between 229 and 295 species. All collected
   morphospecies and species were documented with 2,233 digital images
   available at www.unamfcaracnolab.com. These images are intended to
   expedite species identification and to allow comparisons of taxa not
   formally described. Morphospecies identifications included: 91 species,
   12 as similar to a described species, 86 to genus and 16 to family.
   Differences between seasonality and species collected revealed that
   March and June were similar in composition and were better represented
   in both number of species and adult specimens than August and November,
   although the collecting effort was the same. The similarity ranged
   between 0.35 and 0.71 among seasons. All Rights Reserved (C) 2016
   Universidad Nacional Autonoma de Mexico, Instituto de Biologia.},
