Month = {MAY 1},
Note = {Symposium on Laser Interaction with Advanced Materials: Fundamentals and
   Applications, Lille, FRANCE, 2014},
Abstract = {In this work, we present results on texturing a 500 nm thick bismuth
   film, deposited by sputtering onto a glass slide using a low-cost
   homemade, near-infrared pulsed laser platform. A 785 nm laser diode of a
   CDDVD pickup head was precisely focused on the sample mounted on a
   motorized two-axis translation stage to generate localized surface
   microbumps on the bismuth films. This simple method successfully
   transferred desired micropatterns on the films in a computer-numerical
   control fashion. Irradiated zones were characterized by atomic force
   microscopy and scanning electron microscopy. It was observed that final
   results are strongly dependent on irradiation parameters. (C) 2014
   Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.},
