Abstract = {Using collinear reversible configurations and some properties of
   symmetry we obtain horseshoe periodic orbits in the general planar
   three-body problem with masses m(1) >> m(2) >= m(3), which usually
   represents a system formed by a planet and two small satellites; for
   instance, the system Saturn-Janus-Epimetheus. For the numerical analysis
   we have taken the values m(2)/m(1) = 3.5 x 10(-4) and m(3)/m(1) = 9.7 x
   10(-5) corresponding to 10(5) times the mass ratios of Saturn-Janus and
   Saturn-Epimetheus, respectively.},
