   Basicas \& Ingeniera; UAM Istapalapa, Dept Matemat; Univ Nacl Autonoma
   Mexico; UNAM, Fac Ciencias; UNAM, Coordinac Invest; Consejo Nacl Ciencia
   \& Technol; Benemerita Univ Autonoma Puebla; Soc Matemat Mexicana},
Abstract = {Let X be a continuum and 2(X) be the hyperspace of all nonempty closed
   subsets of X endowed with the Hausdorff metric. It is known that for
   each continuous map f : X -> X the density of periodic points of the
   induced map 2(f) : 2(X) -> 2(X) implies the density of periodic points
   of the base map f provided that X is a graph. In this note we describe a
   continuum X and a continuous map f : X -> X where the density of
   periodic points of the induced map 2f does not imply the density of
   periodic points of the base map f. Also we study a condition of f
   equivalent to the density of periodic points of 2(f)},
