Month = {OCT-DEC},
Abstract = {This paper presents two extensions of the second order polymorphic
   lambda calculus, system F, with monotone (co) inductive types supporting
   (co) iteration, primitive (co) recursion and inversion principles as
   primitives. One extension is inspired by the usual categorical approach
   to programming by means of initial algebras and final coalgebras;
   whereas the other models dialgebras, and can be seen as an extension of
   Hagino's categorical lambda calculus within the framework of parametric
   polymorphism. The systems are presented in Curry-style, and are proven
   to be terminating and type-preserving. Moreover their expressiveness is
   shown by means of several programming examples, going from usual data
   types to lazy codata types such as streams or infinite trees.},
