   Superiores Monterrey; Sun Microsyst; Microsoft},
Abstract = {Gamma is a simple, but powerful, parallel programming language. Its only
   data structure is the multiset or bag. Banatre and Metayer proposed the
   language as a means to derive sistematically programs in the spirit of
   Dijkstra's discipline of programming. It has been applied to solve
   problems in scheduling, image processing and fractal generation.
   Different operational semantics models for Gamma have been proposed. We
   single out one of them and also produce a denotational semantics for
   which full abstraction is proven with respect to the operational model
   chosen. The result can be used as a basis for a further proof system for
   Gamma.},
