   International-Society-for-History-Philosophy-and-Social-Studies-of-Biolo
   gy, SEATTLE, WASHINGTON, JUL, 1997},
Organization = {Int Soc Hist Philos \& Social Studies Biol},
Abstract = {The emergence and development of `national sciences' in Latin American
   countries were not, until very recently, part of the agenda of
   historians of science be cause the `traditional' history of sciences was
   not interested in the scientific activity of peripheral areas. The
   history of science is a recent discipline in Mexican historiographic
   studies. The methodological interest in the history of science, the
   creation of schools and institutes that deal with it, the establishment
   of particular chairs, the organization of national societies, and the
   publication of books and periodicals are all very recent. It is
   important to carry out studies in the history of science that examine
   the development of Mexican science introducing the `local' context, and
   study how this development has influenced the formation of scientific
   societies and the development of scientific disciplines in the country.
   We want to explore the introduction of genetics in Mexico as applied to
   agriculture between 1930 and 1960. This matter has not been investigated
   in Mexico and therefore this work would represent one of the first
   studies of this subject and one of the first studies in the general
   field of Mexican scientific history.},
