Abstract = {Seeds of two maize strains, one resistant and the other susceptible to
   Armyworm (Spodoptera frugiperda J. E. Smith) and to Southwestern corn
   borer (Diatraea grandiosella Dyar), were sown in the field and the
   plants were artificially infested with neonatal larvae of the two
   insects.
