   of the seeds at room temperature and at 5 degrees C. During this period
   the amount of oil in the seeds (except in A. religiosa) decreased,
   slightly more in the samples stored at room temperature.
   The fatty acid composition of the oil was not altered by storage, except
   in Alnus firmifolia, where a decrease of linoleic acid and an increase
